# === Engine: Godot ===
# Two subtleties, both of which produced a silently-wrong rule before this:
#  1. A pattern with an internal `/` is anchored to THIS directory, so `.godot/*`
#     would only match a top-level `.godot` and miss `examples/<game>/.godot`.
#     `**/` makes it match at any depth.
#  2. Git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded, so
#     `**/.godot/` plus a `!` negation is inert. Exclude the CONTENTS instead.
**/.godot/*
# ...except the script class registry. `class_name` declarations resolve from this
# one file, so on a FRESH CLONE every script referencing a class_name fails to
# parse — while `godot --headless --path . --quit` still exits 0, so no CI check
# catches it. Fresh clones hit this trap reliably.
# Keep this un-ignore, or run `godot --headless --import` once after cloning.
!**/.godot/global_script_class_cache.cfg
*.translation
export_presets.cfg
# Uncomment if using Godot:
# *.import

